.TH snip-config 1 "" "snip 0.6.2" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-config \- inspect and modify snip configuration
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip config\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip config path\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip config show\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip config init\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip config set\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
\fBsnip config unset\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Inspect and modify the user configuration. path prints the resolved config file, show prints effective stored values, init creates a file, set updates one supported key, and unset removes a key so the built\-in default applies again.
.PP
Unknown TOML fields are preserved when snip writes the file. Configuration key meanings and defaults are documented in snip\-config(5).
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip config"
Inspect and modify ~/.config/snip/config.toml
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip config path"
Print the resolved config file path
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip config show"
Print the current config (defaults to an empty schema when absent)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip config init"
Create a config file, optionally binding a default library
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip config set"
Set one supported config key
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Configuration key to update
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default\-library: Selects the fallback library after command\-line, environment, and ancestor discovery.
.IP \(bu 2
output: Selects the default command output format.
.IP \(bu 2
color: Controls colored command output.
.IP \(bu 2
preview\-render: Selects the default preview renderer.
.IP \(bu 2
preview\-pager: Controls whether previews use a pager.
.IP \(bu 2
editor: Sets the external editor command.
.IP \(bu 2
editor\-cwd: Selects the working directory used by the external editor.
.IP \(bu 2
gui\-editor: Sets the GUI editor command used by open and TUI external\-app actions.
.IP \(bu 2
pager: Sets the pager command used when PAGER is absent.
.IP \(bu 2
default\-language: Sets the language assigned by create when no language is supplied.
.IP \(bu 2
default\-folder: Sets the folder assigned by create; an empty value means Uncategorized.
.IP \(bu 2
default\-tags: Sets the tags assigned by create when no tags are supplied.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-theme: Selects automatic, light, dark, or named TUI theme resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-light\-theme: Selects the theme used for the light appearance slot.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-dark\-theme: Selects the theme used for the dark appearance slot.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-sort: Selects the default TUI snippet sort order.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-density: Selects comfortable or compact TUI spacing.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-line\-numbers: Controls the preview line\-number gutter.
.IP \(bu 2
tui\-simplified\-ui: Replaces Powerline caps with square, font\-independent cells.
.IP \(bu 2
git\-auto\-commit\-interval: Sets the automatic commit interval; zero disables scheduled commits and pushes.
.IP \(bu 2
git\-auto\-push: Pushes ahead commits after automatic interval work.
.IP \(bu 2
git\-auto\-pull: Fetches and integrates the upstream during configured TUI startup behavior.
.IP \(bu 2
git\-backup\-on\-quit: Requests an interactive backup before TUI exit.
.RE
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
New value, parsed according to the selected key
.SS "snip config unset"
Remove one supported config key and restore its built\-in default
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Configuration key to remove
.br

.br
